{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776810538,"nonce":"61x2Gtg2o2fPCwzxZDjTnRg4hHI=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAKK9yw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/68","origin":"github"},"title":"Drop costmap topics from udp_bridge forwarding","message":"## Summary\n\nAnalysis of the 2026-04-21 field session shows the bridged costmap topics\nconsume CPU + queue budget but almost nothing reaches the operator, because\na single costmap message exceeds the udp_bridge per-second rate limit and\nmost of it is dropped in-flight.\n\nMeasured over the session main bag (`2026-04-21T13.18.20.995262455`,\n~85 min):\n\n| topic | offered (source) | delivered over WiFi |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `/bizzy/global_costmap/costmap` | 7.6 MB/s avg, 317 MB/s peak | **2.3%** (97 kB/s) |\n| `/bizzy/local_costmap/costmap`  | 4.4 MB/s avg, 67 MB/s peak  | **1.2%** (10 kB/s) |\n\nBy contrast, the compressed camera streams (~1.3 MB/s offered) are\ndelivered at 92–99% on the same link. The costmaps are the dominant\nsource of the ~19% rate-limit drop rate on WiFi.\n\n## Proposed Change\n\nRemove the two costmap entries from the bridge's forwarded topics in\n`bizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\n# Lines to remove from the bridged topics list and `remotes: operator:` block\n- local_costmap\n- global_costmap\n  ...\n  global_costmap: {source: global_costmap/costmap, period: 3.0}\n  local_costmap:  {source: local_costmap/costmap,  period: 3.0}\n```\n\nKeep `local_costmap_footprint` (small, informational) and everything else\nthat's delivering well.\n\n## Context\n\n- Analyzed bag: `~/data/logs/bizzyboat/2026-04-21T13.18.20.995262455`\n- Full per-topic stats: `.agent/scratchpad/udp_bridge_topics_2026-04-21.csv`\n  in the ros2_agent_workspace scratchpad\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- **Costmap downsampling / compression relay** — if operator-side ever\n  needs costmaps, a separate downsample node or compressed representation\n  would be the right approach; not pursued now.\n- **udp_bridge resend-timer investigation** — both WiFi and VPN showed\n  matching ~22% retransmit rates, suggesting a bridge-internal timing\n  issue worth a follow-up issue in `rolker/udp_bridge`. Separate ticket.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}